  "title": "Artemis I Leaders Discuss Orion Return, Preview Recovery Operations Dec. 5, 2022",
  "description": "Leaders from NASA present an overview of the return powered flyby (RPF) burn of the Orion vehicle on December 5. RPF, which occurred earlier in the day, committed Orion to a return to Earth trajectory. Orion is completing an uncrewed test flight to check out key vehicle systems as part of the Artemis I mission and is slated to splashdown off the coast of California on December 11, completing a 25.5 day mission.  Get the latest from NASA weekly: www.nasa.gov/subscribe",
